{"message":"fix(a11y): visible focus ring on modal-input; dialog semantics + focus-trap/Escape/restore on auth modal\n\nmodal-input's outline:none had no :focus-visible replacement -- only a\nborder-color change on :focus, easy to miss for keyboard users, across\nevery hand-rolled modal form field (create/rename channel, etc).\n\nauthModal (auth.showModal/hideModal in wireweave-bridge.js) was the one\nreal, reachable overlay with zero dialog semantics: no role/aria-modal,\nno focus-trap, no Escape-to-close, no focus-restore to the trigger --\nlive-witnessed via cdp before the fix (role/aria-modal both null, focus\nleft on the trigger button after open). Added _a11yPersistentModal in\nnostr-channels-ui.js, the same contract as the existing _a11yModal but\nfor a modal toggled via style.display rather than appended/removed per\nopen, and wired it into showModal/hideModal.\n\nVerified live: prior focus-race, Voice Settings dialog semantics, and\nAlt+ArrowUp/Down drag-reorder keyboard-equivalent fixes documented in\nAGENTS.md all still hold -- no regression found in this sweep.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","paths":["docs/css/zellous.css","docs/js/nostr-channels-ui.js","docs/js/wireweave-bridge.js"],"SESSION_ID":"a11y-sweep-1789939915"}
